ncounter the magician in reverse  but very importantly the magician is  often associated with beginnings which  makes an awful lot of sense because  magician's red was the very first dance  scene in its full glory in jojo's  bizarre adventure now as for what this  fire birdie can do  let's take a look at some stats and  initially the stand could seem  a bit underwhelming having scored a b in  power speed and durability whilst  attaining a c  in range and precision whilst invoking a  shameful d  in its developmental potential it's  fairly solid in general though i mean  it's not the paragon of perfection that  star platinum was but magician's red is  more than a passing grade we'll uh we'll  give it that  in regards to power there's nothing  really to be complaining about with a b  and magicians red has demonstrated some  pretty fearsome combative force  such as when it was able to shatter the  armor of another stand judgment with a  mere singular kick  and as much as i don't want to put too  much stock into letters judgment had a b  rating and durability so we are looking  pretty good for magicians right here  however unlike many of the other punch  ghosts magicians red primarily showcases  its power through projectile flame  attacks  a great example of which would be a  crossfire hurricane during which time a  stand is able to conjure a series of  flaming arcs to be fired at an enemy  with each resulting in some pretty damn  devastating damage upon impact however  this is far from a simple blunt big old  projectile because the stand is also  capable of adapting this technique to  cover a much larger area or deal with  copious amounts of opponents if need be  through the crossfire hurricane special  in vacation which does see magicians red  conjo and arc but then split it into  many many smaller arcs for a greater  area of effect style attack and also  just in case you're not familiar an arc  is an egyptian hieroglyphic  that is used to represent life and as  such the possession of one can be seen  as an extension of life or at the very  least that was the idea i don't actually  know how well that worked for the  ancient egyptians probably not great  since they're all dead but i do quite  like how it is incorporated into  magicians red  as a more offensive technique rather  than a preservation of life there's a  nice siren either this actually goes all  the way back to horus though because his  eyes were said to be made up of the  morning star and the evening star aka  the sun and the moon the morning star  representing power whilst the evening  star signified healing so in many ways  the super basic attack from magician's  red  actually perfectly encapsulates the idea  of horus by summoning that overwhelming  flame power  in the shape of the symbol of life very  classic archy thought given to this one  here in regards to speed magicians red  is also nothing to scoff at because  while it is certainly not touted to move  at the speed of light like say star  platinum it was more than capable of  facing off against paul nara's silver  chariot which was  granted an a ranking in the realm of  speed a lot of this was of course due to  avdor's more strategic use of magician's  red  in order to make up for the gap that did  exist but that does display that this  stand  does possess a fairly incredible amount  of speed for that to even be an option  meanwhile it's not the greatest strength  is that of durability magicians red can  take quite the beating but we should  start to delve into some negatives here  which do present themselves in the range  category magician's red is of course a  close range stand  very similar to that of star platinum it  has a very narrow effective range  although it should be noted that since  its attacks are primarily projectile  based then this is much less of an issue  magicians red can just stick with abdul  all day long and fire anks wildly at  whatever opponent we may have this does  however bring up the issue of precision  you may have noticed this by now but  this stand is not  at all designed for subtle attacks fire  is a very unruly substance after all and  avdol tends to command it to its full  destructive potential  meaning that magician's red is a very  all or nothing endeavor in fact even its  specialty attack crossfire hurricane  special is simply designed to increase  the area of damage caused  rather than provide any sort of handy  utility and that brings us to by far the  worst category of magicians red which is  a very sad d  in developmental potential which  essentially means that what we see  is what we get which isn't to say that  it's impossible to push magician spread  further because you know it's not an  e-ranking at least but we're certainly  not going to see something like  magicians red act 2 or magicians read  the world  with that in mind given its low  potential i actually think that avdol is  a fairly amazing wielder of this stand  because he has managed to conjure a neat  little set of powers one of which would  be the red rough rope which spawns  flames designed to restrain an opponent  rather than to burn or hurt them  although the idea is also that  eventually the flames will burn all of  the oxygen around the target and  potentially lead to their suffocation  yay but here is where we see avdol make  the absolute most of that c  in precision because this is some fairly  subtle control over magician's red  reducing the immediate impact of the  flames  as well as moulding them into a  particular sort of semi-permanent shape  and another fascinating use of the stand  by abdul would be the life detector  technique whereby magicians red can  produce a heat radar capable of  detecting movements breathing  and even stand energy which is pretty  insane although that one time it was put  to usables against an opponent who hard  counted it entirely by having access to  another dimension  some more fun facts about magicians red  while this stand itself appeared in the  time before they were widely named after  various pieces of popular music the  signature attack of magicians red being  crossed by a hurricane was taken from  the opening line of jump and jack flash  by the rolling stones  and interestingly but irrelevantly  enough both jumping jack flash and  rolling stones would go on to be future  stand names in part 6 and 5 respectively  for a bit of a bizarre design change  though  magicians red looked ever so slightly  different in the ova incarnation of  jojo's bizarre adventure  in which it sports feathers around its  wrists rather than bracelets  as well as feathers that sprout further  down its neck and i have no idea why  these changes were made but i suppose  someone really wanted to dive into that  whole bird motif although the beak is  also a bit shorter so  i don't know scratch that idea and for  an even more useless fact  originally magician's red was a barefoot  stand however after abdul's return into  the story after the whole  fake out death ordeal from their  non-magician's red was seen wearing  arabian shoes  so it looks like avdor was not the only  one who was busy shopping during their  absence in part three now as for my  personal thoughts on magicians red i'll  be real i was kind of underwhelmed by my  first experience of it when i was going  through stardust crusaders  although to be fair at the time i had no  idea what to expect i was still very  much in that hum on mindset and all of a  sudden there was a big  bird ghost thing but i did grow to enjoy  the stand quite a lot and very rapidly  as well  after the concept of stance in general  became much more familiar to me i do  wish that magicians red had gotten a bit  more time to shine in the series  i mean it's peak was probably when avdor  was facing off against polynomial and  silver chariot  but that was an incredibly early moment  in the series and after that almost  every time it was summoned it just felt  like going through the motions with it  although to be fair you could probably  say that about quite a few part three  stands  really magician's red in my mind suffers  from the simplicity of stardust  crusaders it was the very first stand  showcased at the very dawn of this  concept that would eventually spiral  into this endlessly fascinating group of  existences which do make magicians red  seem incredibly  underwhelming in comparison and in  retrospect i do wish that archie had  taken a bit more advantage of the horus  inspiration and maybe equipped magicians  red with some sort of degree of healing  like maybe some blue phoenix flames or  something just to give it a bit more  depth although that probably would have  seemed quite overpowered in part three  so  uh look i guess it's fine for what it is  but where does that leave us here today  well despite my personal feelings there  is no denying that this is a solid and  sturdy stand  if you are looking for a punch ghost and  star platinum is not available then this  is a great choice because it does come  with that degree of raw power  and mild utility but mild is better than  none  and there are some stands who have  absolutely none but yeah i would never  go so far as to call this stand  particularly  versatile it has a very straightforward  purpose which is to engage in  destructive based combat which i do have  to wonder how often abdul did prior to  the events part three  i mean before dio anya went wild with  the stand arrows stand users would have  been pretty damn read to stumble across  although i can't deny that being able to  instantly summon a firebird is a nice  piece of comfort to have in the back of  your mind  during any stage of life and with that i  think we can officially add magicians  red to the stand  encyclopedia but what do you guys think  of magicians red please do let me know  down in the comments below or even join  my discord server and if you're keen for  some more jojo content then please do go  and check out some of my other videos or  even subscribe to the channel the  regular jojo wonder delivered straight  into your youtube feed but for now this  has been the new world review  and i'll see you next time

